abstract: >
  The Autonomous Constitutional Framework (ACF) is a governance and engineering
  framework for autonomous AI systems, centered on constitutional protocols,
  cryptographic identity binding, substrate-independent state persistence, and
  storage-layer enforcement of framework invariants. The public repository
  contains manifesto documents, protocol specifications, reference
  implementations, research papers, and governance case studies. Portions of
  the framework's operational apparatus are held from public distribution per
  the standing REDACTIONS-AND-ATTRIBUTIONS declaration.
